  "snapshot": {
    "$defs": {
      "CertifiedRef": {
        "description": "Which certified version supplied a piece of meaning in this snapshot.\n\nM24: `apply_certified` applied `rec.payload` and dropped `rec.envelope`, so mnemiq carried the\nCONTENT of a certified record and could not say which VERSION produced it -- and an emitted\ntrace could therefore never name what it relied on. Verity D131 is the mirror: it kept the\nreference at ingest and threw it away.\n\nDeliberately a list of typed refs rather than a `{object_id: version}` dict. `object_id` does\nnot identify a record -- `loss_ratio` is legitimately both the metric and the glossary\ndefinition (Verity D124 was exactly that mistake) -- and this shape is already the wire type\nthe trace carries, so it crosses without translation.",
        "properties": {
          "object_id": {
            "title": "Object Id",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "object_type": {
            "title": "Object Type",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "version_hash": {
            "title": "Version Hash",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "object_type",
          "object_id",
          "version_hash"
        ],
        "title": "CertifiedRef",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "CodeScheme": {
