      "Narrowed": {
        "description": "One object the access decision narrowed, as it reaches a consumer.\n\nMirrors `sql.rls.Narrowing` across the contract boundary. The flags mean exactly what that\ntype's field comments say -- in particular `columns` is \"the query referenced a column name\nthis table masks\", which is neither \"your answer lost a column\" nor \"the rewrite masked\nsomething\". Do not restate them here; one contract, one place.\n\nThe vocabulary is deliberate: this docstring reaches the OPEN contract schema, which bans the\npaid plane's terms outright (`tests/test_contract_schema.py`). An earlier draft used the paid\nword for access rules and failed that test -- twice, because the note explaining the failure\nused the word again. The boundary is enforced on words, in the artifact other systems read.",
        "properties": {
          "columns": {
            "title": "Columns",
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "object": {
            "title": "Object",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "rows": {
            "title": "Rows",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "object",
          "rows",
          "columns"
        ],
        "title": "Narrowed",
        "type": "object"
